% -----------------------------------------------------------------
\section{Conclusion}

FiLMUNet demonstrates that conditioning an interferogram denoising network on acquisition geometry is the key enabler for handling geometry-diverse Capella Space stacks. Self-supervised training via sub-look Noise2Noise combined with closure-consistency and temporal stack losses removes the need for labeled reference data, while predicted aleatoric uncertainty propagates to SNAPHU and SBAS to improve the full InSAR processing chain. Ablation confirms that both the closure loss and FiLM conditioning contribute independently to the M1 and M5 improvements; removing either degrades performance, particularly for pairs at extreme incidence angles. The entire pipeline is reproducible from the public Capella Space S3 dataset (STAC endpoint and SHA-256 checksums provided in \texttt{REPRODUCIBILITY.md}).

